==Selection Process==
On 19<sup>th</sup> February, 2024, ''King Pro League'' (KPL) published a preview of the selection process for the ''KPL Dream Team''. In the preview poster, the Dream Team will act as KPL's global representative, representing the league's "historical glory, abilities, and influence", and aims to spread "the spirit of Honor of Kings esports". They will also act as "''KPL brand ambassadors''" when representing the KPL in the international tournaments.<ref name="Selection Preview">{{cite web|url=https://weibo.com/6074356560/O1lsPv96U|title=【2024 KPL梦之队选拔信息】抢先看！|trans_title=2024 KPL Dream Team Selection Information - Preview!|author=[[King Pro League]]|date=2024-02-19|language={{Flag|cn}} Chinese}}</ref>

The selection will be done through a voting process by fans and a ''Professional Team''. All players who were part of the roster for any of the 16 ''Fixed Seat'' (franchise) teams in the [[King Pro League/2024/Spring|KPL 2024 Spring split]] wil be eligible to be nominated to be part of the Dream Team.<ref name="Selection Preview"/><ref name="Selection Process">{{cite web|url=https://weibo.com/6074356560/O1lsPv96U|title=#2024KPL王者梦之队# 选拔将于5月20日12:00正式开启！|trans_title=2024 KPL Dream Team Selection will officially begin on 20th May 12 noon!|author=[[King Pro League]]|date=2024-04-29|language={{Flag|cn}} Chinese}}</ref> In addition, coaches who self-nominate to contest for the coaching spot, registered (current or formerly) as a head coach in the KPL, and passed the ''2024 KPL Coach Qualifying Test'', will be eligible to become coach of the Dream Team.

During the voting period (20<sup>th</sup> - 27<sup>th</sup> May), fans will be given 2 votes daily - 1 for player, and 1 for coach - to vote for who they think deserves to be on the KPL Dream Team. In addition, there is an opportunity to complete daily tasks to collect an additional 2 votes, as well as a "warm-up task" to collect 4 votes (2 for player and 2 for coach) prior to the voting period.<ref name="Selection Process" /> The votes as tabulated will make up the "Fan Voting" ranking. In addition, a 43-member team, comprising the Organising Committee, official casters and hosts, partnered Content Creators and Media outlets, and representatives from the KPL clubs, will cast votes to make up the "''Professional Team''" ranking.<ref name="Selection Process" />

At the end of the voting period, the players will be ranked accordingly, taking the average of their rank position in the "Fan Voting" ranking and the "''Professional Team''" ranking, tie-broken by the latter.<ref name="Selection Process" /> The top player in each position, the 5 highest-ranked players (outside of the top in each position), and the top 2 coaches, will be selected to make up the 12-man Dream Team.<ref name="Selection Preview" /><ref name="Selection Process" />

